この記事では、短命なアクセストークンと長寿命なリフレッシュトークンを使用した、クリーンで柔軟なデュアルトークン認証システムの実装を紹介します。

この実装は以下の3つの主要な要素で構成されています：

- アクセストークンとリフレッシュトークンを発行・検証するバックエンド
- 認証状態を管理するためにReduxを使用するフロントエンド
- トークンの有効期限切れを自動的に処理し、リクエストを再試行するインターセプター

アクセストークンは短命（約15分）で、ヘッダー経由で送信されます。一方、リフレッシュトークンは長寿命（約7日）で、HTTP-onlyクッキーに保存されます。

バックエンドはすべてのリクエストに対して標準化されたエラーコードを返します：

- `invalid_request`
- `invalid_token`
- `expired_token`
- `malformed_token`

このパターンは以下のような場合に特に有効です：

- 長寿命トークンをJavaScriptに保存せず、安全にセッション管理を行いたい場合
- スケーラブルで予測可能な認証フローを構築したい場合

## Step 1: トークン戦略の概要

2種類のトークンを使用します：

- **アクセストークン**
  - 短命（約15分）
  - メモリ（Redux）に保存
  - `Authorization`ヘッダーで送信
- **リフレッシュトークン**
  - 長寿命（約7日）
  - HTTP-onlyクッキーに保存
  - 新しいアクセストークンを生成するためのみに使用

この分離により、セキュリティリスクを最小化しつつ、ユーザビリティを維持できます。

## Step 2: バックエンド – トークン生成

ログイン時に両方のトークンを生成します。

```typescript
// utils/helpers.ts
import jwt from "jsonwebtoken";

const ACCESS_SECRET = "access_secret";
const REFRESH_SECRET = "refresh_secret";

export function generateTokens(userId: string) {
  const accessToken = jwt.sign({ userId }, ACCESS_SECRET, {
    expiresIn: "15m",
  });

  const refreshToken = jwt.sign({ userId }, REFRESH_SECRET, {
    expiresIn: "7d",
  });

  return { accessToken, refreshToken };
}
```

## Step 3: リフレッシュトークンの保存（簡易実装）

シンプルにするため、リフレッシュトークンは `data.json` に保存します。

```typescript
// data.json
{
  "refreshTokens": []
}
```

```typescript
// utils/helpers.ts
import fs from "fs";

export function saveRefreshToken(token: string) {
  const data = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync("data.json", "utf-8"));
  data.refreshTokens.push(token);
  fs.writeFileSync("data.json", JSON.stringify(data));
}

export function isValidRefreshToken(token: string) {
  const data = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync("data.json", "utf-8"));
  return data.refreshTokens.includes(token);
}
```

## Step 4: ログインルート

ログイン時の処理：

- トークンを生成
- リフレッシュトークンを保存
- アクセストークンをレスポンスで返す
- リフレッシュトークンをHTTP-onlyクッキーとして設定

```typescript
// login.route.ts
import { serialize } from "cookie";

app.post("/login", (req, res) => {
  // 簡易化のため、userIdを直接受け取っています
  // 実際の本番環境では認証処理を行う必要があります
  const { userId } = req.body;

  const { accessToken, refreshToken } = generateTokens(userId);

  saveRefreshToken(refreshToken);

  const cookie = serialize("refreshToken", refreshToken, {
    httpOnly: true,
    path: "/",
    maxAge: 7 * 24 * 60 * 60,
    sameSite: "strict",
    secure: false, // 本番では true（HTTPS）
  });

  res.setHeader("Set-Cookie", cookie);

  res.json({ accessToken });
});
```

## Step 5: ミドルウェア – アクセストークン検証

すべての保護されたルートでアクセストークンを検証し、構造化されたエラーを返します。

```typescript
// auth.middleware.ts
export function authMiddleware(req, res, next) {
  const authHeader = req.headers.authorization;

  if (!authHeader) {
    return res.status(400).json({ code: "invalid_request" });
  }

  const token = authHeader.split(" ")[1];

  if (!token) {
    return res.status(400).json({ code: "malformed_token" });
  }

  try {
    const decoded = jwt.verify(token, ACCESS_SECRET);
    req.user = decoded;
    next();
  } catch (err: any) {
    if (err.name === "TokenExpiredError") {
      return res.status(401).json({ code: "expired_token" });
    }

    return res.status(401).json({ code: "invalid_token" });
  }
}
```

## Step 6: リフレッシュトークンエンドポイント

アクセストークンが期限切れの場合、フロントエンドは `/refresh` を呼び出します。

```typescript
// refresh.route.ts
import { parse } from "cookie";

app.post("/refresh", (req, res) => {
  const cookies = parse(req.headers.cookie ?? "");
  const token = cookies.refreshToken;

  if (!token) {
    return res.status(401).json({ code: "invalid_request" });
  }

  if (!isValidRefreshToken(token)) {
    return res.status(401).json({ code: "invalid_token" });
  }

  try {
    const decoded = jwt.verify(token, REFRESH_SECRET);

    const newAccessToken = jwt.sign(
      { userId: decoded.userId },
      ACCESS_SECRET,
      { expiresIn: "15m" }
    );

    res.json({ accessToken: newAccessToken });
  } catch {
    return res.status(401).json({ code: "expired_token" });
  }
});
```

## Step 7: フロントエンド – Redux Auth Slice

アクセストークンはReduxで管理します。

```typescript
// auth.slice.ts
import { createSlice } from "@reduxjs/toolkit";

const authSlice = createSlice({
  name: "auth",
  initialState: {
    accessToken: null as string | null,
  },
  reducers: {
    setToken: (state, action) => {
      state.accessToken = action.payload;
    },
    clearToken: (state) => {
      state.accessToken = null;
    },
  },
});
export const { setToken, clearToken } = authSlice.actions;
export default authSlice.reducer;
```

## Step 8: Axiosインターセプター – トークン付与

```typescript
import axios from "axios";
import store from "./store";
import { setToken, clearToken } from "./authSlice";

const api = axios.create({
  baseURL: "/api",
  withCredentials: true,
});

api.interceptors.request.use((config) => {
  const token = store.getState().auth.accessToken;

  if (token) {
    config.headers.Authorization = `Bearer ${token}`;
  }

  return config;
});
```

## Step 9: レスポンスインターセプター（自動リフレッシュ）

```typescript
api.interceptors.response.use(
  (res) => res,
  async (error) => {
    const originalRequest = error.config;

    if (error.response?.data?.code === "expired_token") {
      try {
        const res = await axios.post("/api/refresh", {}, { withCredentials: true });

        store.dispatch(setToken(res.data.accessToken));

        originalRequest.headers.Authorization = `Bearer ${res.data.accessToken}`;

        return axios(originalRequest);
      } catch {
        store.dispatch(clearToken());
      }
    }

    return Promise.reject(error);
  }
);
```

## Step 10: 使用例

```typescript
const fetchUser = async () => {
  const res = await api.get("/me");
  return res.data;
};
```

アクセストークンが期限切れの場合：

- バックエンドが `expired_token` を返す
- インターセプターが `/refresh` を呼び出す
- 新しいアクセストークンを保存
- 元のリクエストを自動で再実行

## 最終フロー

- ユーザーがログイン
- バックエンドが発行：
  - アクセストークン（レスポンス）
  - リフレッシュトークン（HTTP-onlyクッキー）
- フロントエンドがReduxにアクセストークンを保存
- リクエストはヘッダーにトークンを含める
- 期限切れの場合：
  - `expired_token` が返る
  - `/refresh` を呼び出す
  - リクエストを再試行

## この実装で得られるもの

- セキュアなトークン分離（アクセス / リフレッシュ）
- 自動的なセッション復旧
- Reduxによる状態管理
- 標準化されたバックエンドエラーハンドリング
- クリーンでスケーラブルな構成

すべてを、フロントエンドとバックエンドの責務を分離しながら実現できます。

content.en:
This article presents a clean and flexible implementation of a headless modal component built from scratch in React.

The idea is inspired by the design behind headless component libraries such as Headless UI: separating logic, accessibility, and animation from visual styling so developers can fully control the UI.

This implementation consists of three main parts:

- A custom hook (`useModal`) that manages modal state and accessibility behavior
- A wrapper modal component that handles rendering and animations
- Portal rendering to ensure the modal is mounted outside the normal DOM tree

Animations are powered by Motion, while accessibility behaviors such as focus trapping, scroll prevention, and Escape key closing are implemented manually.

This pattern is particularly useful when:

- You want full styling freedom instead of relying on UI libraries
- You want reusable modal logic that can be shared across components
- You want to guarantee accessibility behaviors such as focus management and keyboard navigation

## Step 1: The `useModal` Hook – Core State and References

We start by creating a hook responsible for controlling the modal state and handling accessibility concerns.

The hook exposes:

- `openModal` – opens the modal
- `closeModal` – closes the modal
- `modalRef` – reference to the modal container
- `triggerRef` – reference to the trigger element
- `isOpen` – modal visibility state

```typescript
interface UseModalProps {
  trapFocus?: boolean;
  preventScroll?: boolean;
}

interface UseModalReturns<T extends HTMLElement, M extends HTMLElement> {
  openModal: () => void;
  closeModal: () => void;
  modalRef: RefObject<M | null>;
  triggerRef: RefObject<T | null>;
  isOpen: boolean;
}
```

This hook allows the modal component to remain headless, while the logic stays isolated and reusable.

## Step 2: Defining Focusable Elements

To properly implement focus trapping, we first define a selector that matches all elements that can receive keyboard focus.

```typescript
const FOCUSABLE_SELECTOR = [
  "a[href]",
  "button:not([disabled])",
  'input:not([disabled]):not([type="hidden"])',
  "select:not([disabled])",
  "textarea:not([disabled])",
  '[tabindex]:not([tabindex="-1"])',
].join(",");
```

This selector allows us to collect all focusable elements inside the modal and control keyboard navigation.

## Step 3: Opening the Modal and Preparing Accessibility Behavior

When the modal opens, several things happen:

- The currently focused element is saved
- Page scrolling can optionally be disabled
- Focus moves to the first focusable element inside the modal
- Keyboard listeners are attached

```typescript
const openModal = useCallback(() => setIsOpen(true), []);
const closeModal = useCallback(() => setIsOpen(false), []);
```

Inside `useEffect`, we manage these behaviors when `isOpen` becomes `true`.

```typescript
useEffect(() => {
  if (!isOpen) return;

  const modal = modalRef.current;

  const handleEscapeKey = (e: KeyboardEvent) => {
    if (e.key === "Escape") closeModal();
  };

  const previousOverflow = document.body.style.overflow;

  if (preventScroll) {
    document.body.style.overflow = "hidden";
  }

  lastActiveElement.current = document.activeElement;
```

This ensures the modal behaves correctly both visually and from a keyboard navigation perspective.

## Step 4: Implementing Focus Trap

To maintain accessibility, keyboard navigation should remain inside the modal while it is open.

```typescript
const handleFocusTrap = (e: KeyboardEvent) => {
  if (e.key !== "Tab" || !trapFocus) return;

  const first = focusables[0];
  const last = focusables[focusables.length - 1];
  const active = document.activeElement as HTMLElement | null;

  if (!active || !modal.contains(active)) {
    e.preventDefault();
    first.focus();
    return;
  }

  if (!e.shiftKey && active === last) {
    e.preventDefault();
    first.focus();
    return;
  }

  if (e.shiftKey && active === first) {
    e.preventDefault();
    last.focus();
  }
};
```

This keeps keyboard navigation cycling within the modal elements.

## Step 5: Cleaning Up on Close

When the modal closes:

- Event listeners are removed
- Scroll behavior is restored
- Focus returns to the original trigger element

```typescript
return () => {
  modal.removeEventListener("keydown", handleFocusTrap);
  window.removeEventListener("keydown", handleEscapeKey);
  document.body.style.overflow = previousOverflow;

  if (lastActiveElement.current instanceof HTMLElement) {
    lastActiveElement.current.focus();
  }
};
```

This ensures the modal behaves correctly in both accessibility and UX terms.

## Step 6: Creating the Modal Wrapper Component

The wrapper component connects the hook logic with rendering.

Key responsibilities:

- Render the trigger element
- Render the modal content
- Handle animations
- Render using a portal

```typescript
interface ModalProps {
  trigger: React.ReactNode;
  children: React.ReactNode;
  trapFocus?: boolean;
  preventScroll?: boolean;
  duration?: number;
}
```

The trigger is wrapped so we can attach the reference and click handler.

```tsx
<TriggerWrapper ref={triggerRef} onClick={openModal}>
  {trigger}
</TriggerWrapper>
```

## Step 7: Rendering the Modal with a Portal

To avoid layout and stacking issues, the modal is rendered directly inside `document.body` using a portal.

```tsx
createPortal(
  <AnimatePresence>
    {isOpen && (
      <FullScreenLayer>
        <ChildrenMotion
          ref={modalRef}
          initial={{ opacity: 0 }}
          animate={{ opacity: 1 }}
          transition={{ duration }}
          exit={{ opacity: 0 }}
          role="dialog"
          aria-modal="true"
        >
          {children}
        </ChildrenMotion>
      </FullScreenLayer>
    )}
  </AnimatePresence>,
  document.body
)
```

This ensures the modal appears above the entire application.

## Final Complete Implementation

- `useModal.ts`

```typescript
import {
  useCallback,
  useEffect,
  useRef,
  useState,
  type RefObject,
} from "react";

const FOCUSABLE_SELECTOR = [
  "a[href]",
  "button:not([disabled])",
  'input:not([disabled]):not([type="hidden"])',
  "select:not([disabled])",
  "textarea:not([disabled])",
  '[tabindex]:not([tabindex="-1"])',
].join(",");

interface UseModalProps {
  trapFocus?: boolean;
  preventScroll?: boolean;
}

interface UseModalReturns<T extends HTMLElement, M extends HTMLElement> {
  openModal: () => void;
  closeModal: () => void;
  modalRef: RefObject<M | null>;
  triggerRef: RefObject<T | null>;
  isOpen: boolean;
}

export default function useModal<T extends HTMLElement, M extends HTMLElement>(
  props?: UseModalProps,
): UseModalReturns<T, M> {
  const { trapFocus = true, preventScroll = true } = props ?? {};
  const triggerRef = useRef<T | null>(null);
  const modalRef = useRef<M | null>(null);
  const lastActiveElement = useRef<Element | null>(null);
  const [isOpen, setIsOpen] = useState<boolean>(false);

  const openModal = useCallback(() => setIsOpen(true), []);

  const closeModal = useCallback(() => setIsOpen(false), []);

  useEffect(() => {
    if (!isOpen) return;
    if (!modalRef.current || !triggerRef.current) return;
    const modal = modalRef.current;
    const handleEscapeKey = (e: KeyboardEvent) => {
      if (e.key !== "Escape") return;
      closeModal();
    };
    const previousOverflow = document.body.style.overflow;
    if (preventScroll) {
      document.body.style.overflow = "hidden";
    }
    lastActiveElement.current = document.activeElement;
    const focusables = Array.from(
      modal.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(FOCUSABLE_SELECTOR),
    ).filter(
      (el) => !el.hasAttribute("disabled") && !el.getAttribute("aria-hidden"),
    );
    focusables[0]?.focus();
    console.log(focusables[0]);
    const handleFocusTrap = (e: KeyboardEvent) => {
      if (e.key !== "Tab" || !trapFocus) return;
      if (focusables.length < 2) return;
      const first = focusables[0];
      const last = focusables[focusables.length - 1];
      const active = document.activeElement as HTMLElement | null;
      if (!active || !modal.contains(active)) {
        e.preventDefault();
        first.focus();
        return;
      }
      if (!e.shiftKey && active === last) {
        e.preventDefault();
        first.focus();
        return;
      }
      if (e.shiftKey && active === first) {
        e.preventDefault();
        last.focus();
        return;
      }
    };
    modal.addEventListener("keydown", handleFocusTrap);
    window.addEventListener("keydown", handleEscapeKey);
    return () => {
      modal.removeEventListener("keydown", handleFocusTrap);
      window.removeEventListener("keydown", handleEscapeKey);
      document.body.style.overflow = previousOverflow;
      if (lastActiveElement.current instanceof HTMLElement) {
        lastActiveElement.current!.focus();
      }
    };
  }, [isOpen, trapFocus, closeModal, preventScroll]);

  return { openModal, closeModal, modalRef, triggerRef, isOpen };
}
```

- `Modal.tsx`

```tsx
import { Box, styled } from "@mui/material";
// I am using Mui for styling, but feel free to use any other library
import useModal from "./useModal";
import { AnimatePresence, motion } from "motion/react";
import { createPortal } from "react-dom";

interface ModalProps {
  trigger: React.ReactNode;
  children: React.ReactNode;
  trapFocus?: boolean;
  preventScroll?: boolean;
  duration?: number;
}

const TriggerWrapper = styled(Box)({
  display: "inline-block",
});

const ChildrenWrapper = styled(Box)({
  display: "inline-block",
  border: "1px solid black",
  zIndex: 999,
  color: "black",
});

const ChildrenMotion = motion.create(ChildrenWrapper);

const FullScreenLayer = styled(Box)({
  position: "fixed",
  width: "100vw",
  height: "100vh",
  inset: 0,
  zIndex: 12,
  display: "flex",
  justifyContent: "center",
  alignItems: "center",
  backdropFilter: "blur(10px)",
});

export default function Modal({
  trigger,
  children,
  trapFocus,
  preventScroll,
  duration = 0.2,
}: ModalProps) {
  const { isOpen, openModal, triggerRef, modalRef } = useModal({
    trapFocus,
    preventScroll,
  });

  return (
    <>
      <TriggerWrapper ref={triggerRef} onClick={openModal}>
        {trigger}
      </TriggerWrapper>
      {createPortal(
        <AnimatePresence>
          {isOpen && (
            <FullScreenLayer>
              <ChildrenMotion
                ref={modalRef}
                initial={{ opacity: 0 }}
                animate={{ opacity: 1 }}
                transition={{ duration }}
                exit={{ opacity: 0 }}
                role="dialog"
                aria-modal="true"
              >
                {children}
              </ChildrenMotion>
            </FullScreenLayer>
          )}
        </AnimatePresence>,
        document.body,
      )}
    </>
  );
}
```

- `Modal.test.tsx`

```tsx
import { afterEach, beforeEach, describe, expect, test } from "vitest";
import {
  act,
  cleanup,
  render,
  renderHook,
  screen,
  waitFor,
  within,
} from "@testing-library/react";
import userEvent from "@testing-library/user-event";
import Modal from "./Modal";
import useModal from "./useModal";

describe("useModal.ts", () => {
  test("modal initial state", () => {
    const { result } = renderHook(() => useModal());
    expect(result.current.isOpen).toBe(false);
  });

  test("hook functionalities", () => {
    const { result } = renderHook(() => useModal());
    act(() => result.current.openModal());
    expect(result.current.isOpen).toBe(true);
    act(() => result.current.closeModal());
    expect(result.current.isOpen).toBe(false);
  });
});

describe("<Modal />", () => {
  let button: HTMLButtonElement;
  let user: ReturnType<typeof userEvent.setup>;
  beforeEach(() => {
    render(
      <Modal trigger={<button>Open Modal</button>} trapFocus preventScroll>
        <div data-testid="container">
          <h2>My Modal</h2>
          <button>Confirm</button>
          <button>Cancel</button>
        </div>
      </Modal>,
    );
    button = screen.getByRole("button", {
      name: /open modal/i,
    });
    user = userEvent.setup();
  });

  afterEach(() => {
    cleanup();
  });

  test("initial mount", () => {
    expect(button).toBeInTheDocument();
    expect(screen.queryByTestId("container")).not.toBeInTheDocument();
  });

  test("opening and closing modal", async () => {
    await user.click(button);
    await waitFor(() =>
      expect(screen.getByTestId("container")).toBeInTheDocument(),
    );

    await userEvent.keyboard("{Escape}");
    await waitFor(() =>
      expect(screen.queryByTestId("container")).not.toBeInTheDocument(),
    );
  });

  test("focus trap", async () => {
    await user.click(button);
    await waitFor(() =>
      expect(screen.getByTestId("container")).toBeInTheDocument(),
    );
    const buttons = within(screen.getByTestId("container")).getAllByRole(
      "button",
    );
    expect(buttons[0]).toHaveFocus();
    await userEvent.tab();
    expect(buttons[1]).toHaveFocus();
    await userEvent.tab();
    expect(buttons[0]).toHaveFocus();
  });
});
```

- Usage Example

```tsx
<Modal
  trigger={<button>Open Modal</button>}
  trapFocus
  preventScroll
>
  <div>
    <h2>My Modal</h2>
    <button>Confirm</button>
    <button>Cancel</button>
  </div>
</Modal>
```

This implementation provides:

- Focus trapping for accessibility
- Escape key closing
- Scroll locking
- Portal rendering
- Animation support

All while keeping visual styling completely customizable.

